<BlogPostEn slug="sell-telegram-gift-fragment" title="How to sell a Telegram gift on Marketplace or Fragment" heading="How to sell a Telegram gift: Marketplace vs Fragment (2026)" crumb="Sell a Telegram gift" tag="Gifts" description="How to sell a Telegram collectible for Stars or through Fragment: the exact steps, Marketplace vs blockchain, pricing, fees, cashing out and scam protection." keywords="sell Telegram gift, Fragment gifts, Telegram Gift Marketplace, sell collectible gift, export Telegram gift TON" publishDate="2026-08-26" uzHref="https://starsjoy.uz/blog/telegram-sovga-sotish-fragment" ruHref="https://starsjoy.uz/ru/blog/telegram-sovga-sotish-fragment" faqs={faqs}>
  <section><p class="post-lead"><strong>Short answer:</strong> there are two ways to sell a collectible Telegram gift. List it for <strong>Stars in Telegram's Gift Marketplace</strong> for the simplest in-app route. Or export it to the blockchain through <strong>Fragment</strong> and sell it for TON. The first keeps value inside Telegram; the second needs 2FA, a wallet and comfort with crypto risk.</p></section>
  <section><p>Since May 2025, Telegram has supported safe collectible resale directly inside the app, so exporting every gift to Fragment is no longer necessary. Choose Marketplace when you want Stars for another gift or digital purchase. Choose Fragment when you specifically need wallet custody or a TON-denominated sale.</p><p>A gift is not guaranteed to rise in value. Collection demand, trait rarity and the TON exchange rate all move. This is a guide to the mechanism, not investment advice.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Which Telegram gifts can be sold?</h2><p>Resale requires a <strong>collectible</strong> with a unique mint number and Model, Backdrop and Symbol traits. A regular gift may first need to be <a href="/blog/telegram-gift-collectible-upgrade">upgraded to a collectible</a>.</p><ul><li><strong>Sell is visible:</strong> list it in the Marketplace for Stars.</li><li><strong>Transfer → Send via Blockchain is visible:</strong> export becomes possible when its lock date passes.</li><li><strong>Convert to Stars is visible:</strong> this is not resale. Telegram destroys the gift and returns fewer Stars than the buying price, subject to an eligibility window.</li></ul></section>
  <section><h2>How do you sell a gift for Stars?</h2><ol><li>Open <strong>My Profile → Gifts</strong>.</li><li>Select the collectible and tap <strong>Sell</strong>.</li><li>Enter the price in Stars and check the final amount you will receive.</li><li>Confirm the listing. A <strong>Sale</strong> label appears and the item becomes searchable.</li><li>If you change your mind before it sells, tap <strong>Unlist</strong>.</li></ol><p>Telegram's technical documentation separates the resale price from the proceeds received by the owner. Treat the confirmation screen as the source of truth; the buyer-facing number is not necessarily your net proceeds.</p></section>
  <section><h2>How do you sell through Fragment?</h2><ol><li>Enable Telegram two-step verification and prepare a TON-compatible wallet.</li><li>Open the collectible under Profile → Gifts.</li><li>Choose <strong>Transfer → Send via Blockchain</strong>.</li><li>On the official Fragment page, connect the wallet and confirm export.</li><li>Once the NFT reaches the wallet, list or auction it on a supported marketplace.</li></ol><p>A gift may show a <strong>can export at</strong> date; it cannot leave Telegram before then. Network and marketplace fees may apply. If you open Fragment manually, verify the exact <strong>fragment.com</strong> domain.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Marketplace or Fragment: which is better?</h2><div class="post-table-wrap"><table class="post-table"><thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Telegram Marketplace</th><th>Fragment / blockchain</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Settlement</td><td>Telegram Stars</td><td>TON</td></tr><tr><td>Requirements</td><td>Telegram account</td><td>2FA, wallet, crypto</td></tr><tr><td>Difficulty</td><td>In-app listing</td><td>Export and extra fees</td></tr><tr><td>Best for</td><td>Spending value in Telegram</td><td>External custody and TON trading</td></tr><tr><td>Main risk</td><td>Pricing too low</td><td>Phishing, seed theft, exchange rate</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Marketplace is enough for most owners. Fragment is useful when blockchain control or TON settlement is the actual goal.</p></section>
  <section><h2>How should you price the gift?</h2><p>Start with the collection floor, then compare items with similar Model, Backdrop, Symbol and mint number. A lower trait percentage means greater rarity. Low or memorable numbers such as #1, #10 and #100 may carry a premium.</p><ul><li>Do not price from a record sale alone; it may have an exceptional trait combination.</li><li>An asking price is not a completed sale. Check trade history where possible.</li><li>For a faster sale, use the lower end of comparable items; if you can wait, start near the middle.</li><li>Include platform fees and the TON rate in any net-proceeds estimate.</li></ul><p>For context, see the <a href="/en/blog/most-expensive-telegram-gifts">most expensive Telegram gifts</a> and the guide to <a href="/en/blog/what-you-can-do-with-telegram-stars">using Telegram Stars</a>.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Can the proceeds become cash?</h2><p><strong>Stars sale:</strong> Stars are designed for gifts, bots, Mini Apps, paid content and other Telegram purchases. Do not assume that a personal Marketplace balance can be sent straight to a bank card.</p><p><strong>TON sale:</strong> a blockchain marketplace pays TON to your wallet. Turning it into local currency may require a lawful exchange or P2P service. Check the rate, fees, identity requirements and local rules before transacting.</p><p>If your goal is simply another gift, the Stars route is usually easier. Users in Uzbekistan can top up Stars in UZS through <a href="https://telegram.me/starsjoybot" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@starsjoybot</a>.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Seven safety rules</h2><ol><li>Use Telegram's Marketplace or fragment.com.</li><li>Never share your seed phrase, login code or 2FA password.</li><li>Do not open a payment link sent by a supposed buyer.</li><li>Confirm payment in Telegram or a blockchain explorer.</li><li>Do not pay an unknown escrow bot an “unlock fee”.</li><li>Double-check the wallet address and network.</li><li>Treat a gift as a collectible whose price can fall, not guaranteed income.</li></ol><p>See the broader guide to <a href="/en/blog/is-buying-telegram-stars-safe">Telegram Stars and scam safety</a>.</p></section>
  <section><h2>The takeaway</h2><p>Telegram Marketplace is the simplest way to sell a collectible for Stars. Fragment exports it to the blockchain and enables TON trading, but adds a wallet, fees and crypto risk. Decide what form of value you actually want, price from comparable completed sales and never hand over account or wallet credentials.</p></section>
